Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:51:35 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] X-H2 controls: mode dial, focus lever (8 directions + push)
 and dial pushes

From the 5.20 firmware and factory config read in the emulator:
- mode dial: 13 positions on ADC 3 (config halfwords 14072..14122);
  confirmed in the emulator (A and M show on the shooting screen);
- focus lever: ADC 14 bands from table 0x1c38c20 (decoder 0x13ff900),
  cardinals in the catalog, diagonals in the board table; push on GPIO 15.6
  active low (gate 0x13ff8dc). The decoder sees directions; the menu cursor
  does not move yet;
- dial pushes on GPIO 0.13/0.14 by the X-T5's wiring (not confirmed);
- q_button maps to the Quick key (the Q rung from the previous patch had
  no emulator key on this base).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
